## Comparison: +page.ts vs +page.server.ts

### 1. **Where Each Runs**

| File | Execution | Behavior |
|------|-----------|----------|
| `+page.ts` (universal) | Server + Browser | Runs on server during SSR, reruns in browser during hydration and client-side navigation (unless `ssr=false`) |
| `+page.server.ts` | **Server only** | Always executes server-side; result is serialized and sent to client |

### 2. **What Each Can Access**

**`+page.server.ts` (`ServerLoadEvent`) — Exclusive access to:**
- `cookies` — read/set session cookies
- `locals` — user data from `handle` hook
- `clientAddress` — client IP address
- `platform` — platform-specific objects (Cloudflare, Netlify, etc.)
- `request` — full HTTP request object

**`+page.ts` (universal `LoadEvent`):**
- Cannot access cookies, locals, or request directly
- Has `data` property containing parent server load results
- Can call `fetch()` from external APIs without server overhead

**Both have access to:**
- `params` — route parameters from URL
- `route` — route ID (e.g., `/[slug]`)
- `url` — full URL object
- `fetch` — enhanced fetch with credential/relative URL support
- `setHeaders` — cache control headers (server-side only)
- `parent()` — access parent layout load data
- `depends()` / `untrack()` — dependency tracking

### 3. **Serialization Constraints**

**`+page.server.ts` — Must be devalue-serializable:**

Can serialize: JSON, `BigInt`, `Date`, `Map`, `Set`, `RegExp`, repeated/cyclical references, and **Promises** (streamed to client)

**Cannot serialize:** Component constructors, custom class instances, stores, functions

**`+page.ts` — No serialization required:**

Can return anything: components, stores, custom classes, functions

---

## Minimal Examples

### +page.server.ts

```typescript
// src/routes/blog/[slug]/+page.server.ts
import * as db from '$lib/server/database';
import type { PageServerLoad } from './$types';

export const load: PageServerLoad = async ({ params, cookies }) => {
	const sessionId = cookies.get('sessionid');

	return {
		post: await db.getPost(params.slug),
		user: await db.getUser(sessionId),
		// Can include promises for streaming
		comments: db.getComments(params.slug)
	};
};
```

### +page.ts (Universal)

```typescript
// src/routes/blog/[slug]/+page.ts
import type { PageLoad } from './$types';

export const load: PageLoad = async ({ params, fetch, parent }) => {
	// Access server load data
	const serverData = await parent();

	// Fetch from external API
	const res = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/posts/${params.slug}`);

	return {
		...serverData, // Include server data
		apiData: await res.json(),
		// Can return non-serializable values
		formatter: new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US')
	};
};
```

### Both Together

```typescript
// src/routes/+page.server.ts
export const load = async () => ({
	isAdmin: true
});

// src/routes/+page.ts
export const load = async ({ data }) => {
	const Component = data.isAdmin 
		? await import('./AdminPanel.svelte')
		: await import('./UserPanel.svelte');

	return {
		component: Component.default
	};
};
```

### Data in +page.svelte

```svelte
<!-- src/routes/+page.svelte -->
<script>
	import { page } from '$app/state';

	let { data } = $props();
</script>

<h1>{data.post.title}</h1>

<!-- Use server data -->
<p>By {data.user.name}</p>

<!-- Handle streamed promises from server load -->
{#await data.comments}
	Loading comments...
{:then comments}
	{#each comments as comment}
		<p>{comment.text}</p>
	{/each}
{/await}

<!-- Use component from universal load -->
{#if data.component}
	<svelte:component this={data.component} />
{/if}
```

---

## Key Distinction

**Use `+page.server.ts` when:** accessing databases, private APIs, secrets, cookies  
**Use `+page.ts` when:** returning non-serializable values (components, stores) or fetching public data  
**Use both when:** combining server data with unserializable values (pass server result to universal load via `data` property)

