Based on the Tailwind CSS v4 docs, here's how **@theme variables map to generated utility classes**:

## Overview

`@theme` variables are CSS custom properties that automatically generate corresponding utility classes. When you define a theme variable in a namespace, Tailwind generates utilities with the same name as the variable.

## Three Variable Namespaces & Generated Utilities

### 1. **--color-* → Color Utilities**
Generates utilities for backgrounds, text, borders, fills, strokes, etc.
- `--color-mint-500` → `bg-mint-500`, `text-mint-500`, `fill-mint-500`, `border-mint-500`

### 2. **--font-* → Font Family Utilities**
Generates font-family utilities.
- `--font-poppins` → `font-poppins`
- `--font-serif` → `font-serif` (default)

### 3. **--spacing-* → Spacing & Sizing Utilities**
Generates utilities for padding, margin, width, height, gaps, etc.
- `--spacing` (base unit) → `px-4`, `py-8`, `max-h-16`, etc.

**Additional namespaces include:**
- `--text-*` → font size utilities (`text-xl`, `text-2xl`)
- `--radius-*` → border radius utilities (`rounded-sm`, `rounded-lg`)
- `--breakpoint-*` → responsive variants (`sm:*`, `md:*`)
- `--shadow-*` → box shadow utilities (`shadow-md`, `shadow-lg`)

## Minimal CSS & HTML Example

**CSS (app.css):**
```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  --color-mint-500: oklch(0.72 0.11 178);
  --font-poppins: Poppins, sans-serif;
  --spacing: 0.25rem;
}
```

**HTML:**
```html
<div class="bg-mint-500 font-poppins px-4 py-8">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">Hello World</h1>
</div>
```

**Generated CSS output:**
```css
:root {
  --color-mint-500: oklch(0.72 0.11 178);
  --font-poppins: Poppins, sans-serif;
  --spacing: 0.25rem;
}

.bg-mint-500 { background-color: var(--color-mint-500); }
.font-poppins { font-family: var(--font-poppins); }
.px-4 { padding-left: calc(var(--spacing) * 4); padding-right: calc(var(--spacing) * 4); }
.py-8 { padding-top: calc(var(--spacing) * 8); padding-bottom: calc(var(--spacing) * 8); }
```

